      "properties": {
        "reported": true,
        "property_type": "both",
        "summary": "DC susceptibility of 4 matches four Dy(III) ions. It is the only analogue showing frequency-dependent out-of-phase χM'' tails below ~5 K, indicating slow magnetization relaxation of an SMM with a small barrier; applied dc field only slightly enhanced χM'' without allowing an energy-barrier fit. Solid-state photoluminescence does not show the expected Dy(III) 4F9/2 → 6H15/2 (~480 nm) and 4F9/2 → 6H13/2 (~575 nm) bands, attributed to paramagnetic quenching.",
